{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "d1e2f3a4-b5c6-7d8e-9f0a-1b2c3d4e5f6a",
    "name": "BidMart — Support Tickets & System Settings",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "New APIs added in the support-tickets + system-settings task.\n\n**Admin credentials (seeded):**\n| Email                | Password    |\n|----------------------|-------------|\n| admin@bidmart.com    | Admin@1234  |\n\n**Seeded support tickets (5 rows):**\n1. Ahmed Al-Rashidi — COMPLAINT — NEW\n2. Sara Al-Otaibi — SUGGESTION — CONTACTED\n3. Mohammed Al-Ghamdi — INQUIRY — UNDER_REVIEW\n4. Noura Al-Zahrani — OTHER — NEW\n5. Khalid Al-Shehri — COMPLAINT — CONTACTED\n\n**Seeded system settings:** exchange rate 3.75, commission 15%, referral 20 SAR, min liquidation 50 SAR, full social media links.\n\n**Recommended run order:**\n1. 🔑 Setup — Login as Admin\n2. 🎫 Support Tickets → List Tickets (auto-sets `ticketId`)\n3. 🎫 Support Tickets → Get Ticket Detail\n4. 🎫 Support Tickets → Update Ticket Status\n5. ⚙️  System Settings → Get Settings\n6. ⚙️  System Settings → Update Settings\n\n**Permissions required:**\n- `admin:contact-messages:view` — list + detail\n- `admin:contact-messages:update` — update status\n- `admin:settings:view` — get settings\n- `admin:settings:update` — update settings\n\nSuper admin bypasses all permission checks."
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000/api/v1",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Base URL including API prefix and version"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Admin JWT — auto-set by Login request"
    },
    {
      "key": "ticketId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "UUID of a support ticket — auto-set by List Tickets"
    }
  ],
  "item": [

    {
      "name": "🔑 Setup — Login",
      "description": "Run first to populate the adminToken variable used by all subsequent requests.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login as Admin",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Has accessToken', () => pm.expect(res.data.accessToken).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "if (res.success && res.data && res.data.accessToken) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('adminToken', res.data.accessToken);",
                  "  console.log('Admin token saved');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "auth", "login"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"admin@bidmart.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Admin@1234\",\n  \"rememberMe\": false,\n  \"deviceId\": \"postman-admin\",\n  \"fcmToken\": \"string\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "description": "Logs in as the seeded super admin. The test script saves `accessToken` into the `adminToken` collection variable used by every subsequent request."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },

    {
      "name": "🎫 Support Tickets",
      "description": "Admin endpoints for viewing and managing user support tickets (contact messages).\n\nAll routes require `admin:contact-messages:view` (list + detail) or `admin:contact-messages:update` (status update).\n\nBase path: /admin/support-tickets",
      "item": [

        {
          "name": "List Tickets — no filters (default)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('success is true', () => pm.expect(res.success).to.equal(true));",
                  "pm.test('data is array', () => pm.expect(res.data).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "pm.test('meta has total', () => pm.expect(res.meta.total).to.be.a('number'));",
                  "pm.test('sorted newest first', () => {",
                  "  if (res.data.length >= 2) {",
                  "    const first = new Date(res.data[0].created_at).getTime();",
                  "    const second = new Date(res.data[1].created_at).getTime();",
                  "    pm.expect(first).to.be.at.least(second);",
                  "  }",
                  "});",
                  "if (res.data && res.data.length > 0) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('ticketId', res.data[0].id);",
                  "  console.log('ticketId set to', res.data[0].id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{adminToken}}" },
              { "key": "Accept-Language", "value": "en" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/support-tickets",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "support-tickets"]
            },
            "description": "Returns the first page (10 items) sorted newest-first. The test script auto-sets `ticketId` from the first result."
          },
          "response": []
        },

        {
          "name": "List Tickets — filter by status NEW",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('all items are NEW', () => {",
                  "  res.data.forEach(t => pm.expect(t.status).to.equal('NEW'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{adminToken}}" },
              { "key": "Accept-Language", "value": "en" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/support-tickets?status=NEW",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "support-tickets"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "status", "value": "NEW", "description": "NEW | CONTACTED | UNDER_REVIEW" }
